    {
      "id": "com.example.random-palette",
      "name": "Random Wallpaper Palette",
      "author": "Atelier Examples",
      "github": "kaizensx",
      "kind": "plugin",
      "version": "1.0.0",
      "summary": "A command and a hot-corner action that give the live wallpaper, Dock and widgets a fresh, harmonious palette.",
      "description": "# Random Wallpaper Palette\n\nOne shortcut, a new mood. Each shuffle picks a hue, then three more a little further round the colour wheel, from deep shadow to bright crest, and applies them to:\n\n- the live wallpaper's palette,\n- the Dock and widget accents,\n- Atelier's own accent.\n\nRun **Random Wallpaper Palette** from the Command palette, or put **Random Palette** on a hot corner.\n\nNot this time? **Revert** in Looks puts back everything from before the first change.\n",
